## Changes from upstream

- The comment on the URL password rule in `patterns.ts` is reworded.
- The marker is renamed to `[JANITOR-REDACTED:<kind>]`: the `mark` function and the `MARK` pattern.
- `MARK` is anchored, so a value counts as a marker only when it is one whole. A global `MARKS` pattern is used to judge the rest of a partly redacted value.
- The URL password rule allows a slash in the password. A value of up to 5 digits followed by `/`, or by a `?` query with an `=`, is skipped as a port. The user part may contain whole markers but no other `[`. A password cannot contain `://`.
- The scheme of the URL password rule is matched by a lookahead and lookbehind at the `://` (`(?=:\/\/)(?<=\b[a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*)(:\/\/)`), not by a prefix `\b([a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*:\/\/)`. The prefix scanned a whole run of scheme characters from every word boundary, which was quadratic (16 KB of `A1-` took 0.5-1.4 s). The URLs that are hidden are the same, with a scheme of any length; the rule's first capture group is now `://`.
- The port skip of the URL password rule scans a query for its `=` with `(?:(?!:\/\/)[^\s@#])*=`, not `[^\s@#]*=`, so the scan ends at the next `://`. For every `://` whose password starts with digits then `?`, the plain class scanned on past every later `://` up to the next whitespace, `@`, `#` or `=`, which was quadratic on a long line without them. The URLs that are hidden are the same: a password cannot contain `://`.
- The 22 token rules of upstream's `TOKENS` list in `patterns.ts` are moved, unchanged, into files under `rules/` by category: `rules/key-material.ts` (private-key, jwt, bearer-token), `rules/cloud.ts` (aws-access-key, the two aws-secret-key rules, aws-session-token, google-api-key), `rules/code-hosts.ts` (the two github-token rules), `rules/ai.ts` (anthropic-key, the three openai-key rules, huggingface-token), `rules/messaging-payments.ts` (slack-token, slack-webhook, the two stripe-key rules) and `rules/dev-services.ts` (npm-token, pypi-token, sendgrid-key). The `Rule` type is moved from `patterns.ts` to `rules/rule.ts`. The files are the janitor's; the rules in them are upstream's. `patterns.ts` still holds `TOKENS`, module-private, listing the rules by name in upstream's order, and exports `TOKEN_ORDER` (each rule's kind and pattern source) for the order test.
- The tests in `tests/patterns.test.ts` are changed to match these, and extended.
- The slash command is renamed to /janitor-secret-shield.

A future upstream sync is a manual merge. The sed file at `reports_dev/secret-shield/upstream-sync.sed.txt` covers only the marker rename.

## Rules taken from other projects

- `slackAppToken`, `slackConfigAccessToken` and `slackConfigRefreshToken` in `rules/messaging-payments.ts` are taken word for word from the gitleaks rules slack-app-token, slack-config-access-token and slack-config-refresh-token (https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks, release v8.30.1, MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2019 Zachary Rice). The only change is that the leading `(?i)` is written as the scoped group `(?i:...)`.
